o this movie and he wasn't the only  Amityville alum to succumb to  superstition associated with the series  the 2005 remake was also the site of  some freakish coincidences such as a  fisherman's body washing up on the set  shore as filming geared up to begin Ryan  Reynolds told movie web a lot of the  crew were waking up at 3:15 in the  morning which was when all these  atrocities in the house took place each  time I think it was a subconscious thing  you read the script and suddenly pop  awake at 3:15 in the morning even if  it's just a coincidence it's still  creepy the box he might be playing a  savage bat slinging brute of the zombie  apocalypse in The Walking Dead but  Jeffrey Dean Morgan got pretty worked up  over his time on the  of the possession he admitted to being  so freaked out by the real history of  the Dybbuk box that they made sure not  to take it lightly during filming he  told I Oh 9 there are some weird  goings-on on set  lots of lightbulbs exploding just  overall kind of creepiness don't mock  the box was sort of the mantra that we  lived by while we were filming this he  purposefully steered clear of the real  box that inspired the film saying  somebody wanted to bring the box to the  set the real box I was adamantly against  it if you go and look at what has  happened to people that have had contact  with an actual Dybbuk box it's not good  stuff why risk that why indeed the clown  capturing the essence of Pennywise the  clown for the cinematic adaptation of  Stephen King's it would be no easy feat  for anyone not only was there a prior  portrayal by Tim Curry to live up to but  unlike most villains there are no human  or redeeming qualities to latch on to to  make an actor feel better about playing  it understandably for Bill skarsgård the  process of suiting up as the child  Slayer was no picnic the actor has said  that the process of spending time with  this character was like a destructive  relationship that he was relieved to end  when 